class:: MIRaPlot
summary:: Whole-audio-file visual display and interactive MIR inspector
categories:: GUI>MIR, Libraries>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa-file-visualization, Classes/MIRaGUI, Classes/MIRaColormap, Classes/MIRaFileAnalyzer

description::
MIRaPlot provides whole-audio-file graphical displays and an interactive multi-tier inspection dashboard, bringing standard Music Information Retrieval (MIR) visual conventions (such as those in librosa, Essentia, and MIRtoolbox) to SuperCollider.

It supports fast Non-Real-Time (NRT) batch extraction of audio files using MIRa's native C++ signal-processing primitives (including link::Classes/PitchYIN::, link::Classes/HPCP::, link::Classes/CQT::, link::Classes/Onsets2::, link::Classes/SpecCentroid2::, and link::Classes/SpecFlatness2::). Matrices are rendered into hardware-accelerated link::Classes/Image:: surfaces with perceptual colormaps (link::Classes/MIRaColormap::).

Visualizations include:
list::
## strong::Waveform & Novelty (waveshow)::: Time-domain envelope peaks with detected onset markers and overlaid RMS contour.
## strong::Spectrogram (spectrogram)::: Constant-Q (CQT) time-frequency transform on a logarithmic frequency grid (default 72 bins, 12 bins/octave) in decibels (dB), complete with frequency ticks and colorbar.
## strong::Chromagram (chromagram)::: 12-pitch-class harmonic pitch profile (HPCP) with semitone labels (C through B) showing pitch distribution over time.
## strong::Pitch Trajectory (pitch)::: Fundamental frequency (F0) contour plotted on a musical MIDI pitch grid (C2 through B6) with voicing confidence.
## strong::Interactive Dashboard (dashboard)::: Synchronized multi-tier stack combining all representations with audio playback, scrubbing cursor, colormap switching, and timecode display.
::

classmethods::

method:: waveshow
Displays a standalone waveform with overlaid onset lines and RMS envelope.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file. Basenames found in MIRa's code::sounds/:: folder are automatically resolved.
argument:: width
Window width in pixels (default: 840).
argument:: height
Window height in pixels (default: 280).
returns:: A link::Classes/Window::.

method:: spectrogram
Displays a 2D time-frequency Constant-Q spectrogram with dB magnitude scaling, frequency ticks, and a colorbar.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file.
argument:: colormap
Symbol naming the colormap: code::\magma:: (default), code::\viridis::, code::\plasma::, code::\inferno::, or code::\coolwarm::.
argument:: width
Window width in pixels (default: 840).
argument:: height
Window height in pixels (default: 360).
returns:: A link::Classes/Window::.

method:: chromagram
Displays a 12-pitch-class harmonic chromagram (HPCP) showing semitones C through B over time.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file.
argument:: colormap
Symbol naming the colormap (default: code::\viridis::).
argument:: width
Window width in pixels (default: 840).
argument:: height
Window height in pixels (default: 320).
returns:: A link::Classes/Window::.

method:: pitch
Displays the extracted fundamental frequency trajectory (F0) on a musical MIDI note grid.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file.
argument:: width
Window width in pixels (default: 840).
argument:: height
Window height in pixels (default: 320).
returns:: A link::Classes/Window::.

method:: dashboard
Launches the synchronized multi-tier MIR File Inspector with audio playback, scrubbing cursor, colormap switching, and time readout.
argument:: audioPath
Path to the audio file.
argument:: colormap
Initial colormap name symbol (default: code::\magma::).
argument:: tiers
Array of tier symbols to display, chosen from code::[\wave, \spec, \chroma, \pitch, \dynamics]::. Defaults to displaying all tiers.
argument:: width
Window width in pixels (default: 960).
argument:: height
Window height in pixels (default: 740).
argument:: title
Custom window title string.
returns:: A link::Classes/Window::.

method:: makeMatrixImage
Renders a 2D float matrix (frames x frequency bins) into a hardware-accelerated link::Classes/Image:: using a specified colormap and optional dB power scaling.
argument:: matrix
2D Array of floats, code::[numFrames][numBins]::.
argument:: colormapName
Colormap symbol.
argument:: dbScale
Boolean. If true, converts linear values to decibels clipped to 80 dB dynamic range.
returns:: An link::Classes/Image::.

method:: drawColorbar
Draws a vertical colorbar legend using link::Classes/Pen::.
argument:: rect
A link::Classes/Rect:: specifying the bounding box.
argument:: colormapName
Colormap symbol.
argument:: topLabel
String label at top of colorbar (e.g. code::"0dB"::).
argument:: bottomLabel
String label at bottom of colorbar (e.g. code::"-80dB"::).

examples::
code::
(
// 1. Full Multi-Tier Interactive MIR File Inspector:
// Displays waveform, CQT spectrogram, HPCP chromagram, pitch contour, and dynamics.
// Click anywhere on the plot to scrub audio playback.
s.waitForBoot({
    var soundPath = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    MIRaPlot.dashboard(soundPath);
});
)
::

code::
(
// 2. Constant-Q Spectrogram with Perceptual Colormap:
s.waitForBoot({
    var soundPath = MIRaGUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    MIRaPlot.spectrogram(soundPath, colormap: \magma);
});
)
::

code::
(
// 3. 12-Pitch-Class Chromagram (HPCP):
s.waitForBoot({
    var soundPath = MIRaGUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    MIRaPlot.chromagram(soundPath, colormap: \viridis);
});
)
::

code::
(
// 4. Waveform with Detected Transient Onsets:
s.waitForBoot({
    var soundPath = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    MIRaPlot.waveshow(soundPath);
});
)
::

code::
(
// 5. Fundamental Frequency (F0) Contour on MIDI Pitch Grid:
s.waitForBoot({
    var soundPath = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    MIRaPlot.pitch(soundPath);
});
)
::
